CHAPTER.VERS:
In that day shall
This song was made to comfort the faithful when their captivity would come, assuring them also of their deliverance, for which they should sing this song. this song be sung in the land of Judah; We have a strong city;
God's protection and defence will be sufficient for us. salvation will [God] appoint [for] walls and bulwarks.

For he bringeth down them that dwell on high; 

          There is no power so high that it can hinder God, when he will deliver his.
         the lofty city, he layeth it low; he layeth it low, [even] to the ground; he bringeth it [even] to the dust.
